  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Use first principles differentiation to find the derivative function $f'(x)$ for $2x^2-20x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f'(x)=4x-20$",
      "worked": "Let $f(x)=2x^2-20x$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}f(x+h)&=2(x+h)^2-20(x+h)\\\\&=2x^2+4xh+2h^2-20x-20h.\\end{aligned}$$\nFor $h\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}&=\\frac{2x^2+4xh+2h^2-20x-20h-(2x^2-20x)}{h}\\\\&=\\frac{4xh+2h^2-20h}{h}\\\\&=4x+2h-20.\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\\\\&=\\lim_{h\\to0}(4x+2h-20)\\\\&=4x-20.\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
